0..75 Comment "// The Rust extern `f(x: Option<&u32>, n: u32) -> u32` as a function row of"
76..138 Comment "// the foreign boundary, admitted against its witness records."
139..141 Comment "//"
142..214 Comment "// A function type means a Hoare triple over its arguments\' and result\'s"
215..293 Comment "// realisers. `Option<&u32>` is realised by the null niche, so `f`\'s triple is"
294..367 Comment "// `deref_or`\'s at `u32`. Each argument\'s and the result\'s witness record"
368..440 Comment "// summarises its realisers, read off its code by Rust\'s default layout."
441..443 Comment "//"
444..519 Comment "// `admit(declared, row)` compares rustc\'s printed layouts with the records"
520..599 Comment "// clause by clause, answering `Admitted` or `Unrealised` with the first clause"
600..672 Comment "// that fails. Each extern below differs from the row in one clause. The"
673..746 Comment "// checker holds the layout program\'s integer comparisons as neutrals, so"
747..774 Comment "// admission is a run here."
775..777 Comment "//"
778..850 Comment "// - see: #2901 — not implemented: the check-time refusal of an extern"
851..898 Comment "//   declaration, `BoundaryUnrealised.<clause>`"
899..977 Comment "// - see: `pathological/interop/boundary/function-row.gandr` — the predicate"
978..1029 Comment "//   chosen through the layout, refused `Undecided`"
1030..1104 Comment "// - see: `model/specification/niche-realizability.gandr` — `deref_or`\'s"
1105..1152 Comment "//   triple and the tagged layout\'s equivalence"
1153..1231 Comment "// - see: `library/std/src/boundary.gandr` — the row, the witness record and"
1232..1244 Comment "//   `admit`"
1245..1311 Comment "// - see: `library/std/src/layout.gandr` — Rust\'s default layout"
1312..1390 Comment "// - see: Wagner, Eisbach and Ahmed, _Realistic Realizability: Specifying ABIs"
1391..1466 Comment "//   You Can Count On_, OOPSLA 2024, doi:10.1145/3689755, § 3.1 and § 4.2"
1468..1542 Comment "// The Rust side, built by rustc 1.98.0-nightly (f28ac764c 2026-06-23) for"
1543..1614 Comment "// x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu. Its layouts are from `rustc --edition 2024"
1615..1683 Comment "// --crate-type=lib -Zprint-type-sizes` over the eight externs, with"
1684..1740 Comment "// `size_of`, `align_of` and `needs_drop` for each type:"
1741..1743 Comment "//"
1744..1771 Comment "//     #[unsafe(no_mangle)]"
1772..1832 Comment "//     pub extern \"C\" fn f(x: Option<&u32>, n: u32) -> u32 {"
1833..1880 Comment "//         match x { Some(r) => *r, None => n }"
1881..1889 Comment "//     }"
1890..1892 Comment "//"
1893..1960 Comment "//     type              size  alignment  discriminant   needs drop"
1961..2020 Comment "//     Option<&u32>      8     8          none (niche)   no"
2021..2080 Comment "//     u32               4     4          -              no"
2081..2140 Comment "//     u64               8     8          -              no"
2141..2200 Comment "//     &u32              8     8          -              no"
2201..2260 Comment "//     Tagged            16    8          -              no"
2261..2321 Comment "//     Option<Box<u32>>  8     8          none (niche)   yes"
2322..2381 Comment "//     Packed            4     1          -              no"
2382..2384 Comment "//"
2385..2463 Comment "// `Tagged` is `#[repr(C)] struct Tagged { tag: usize, ptr: *const u32 }`, the"
2464..2527 Comment "// tagged layout of `Option<&u32>` written out, and `Packed` is"
2528..2604 Comment "// `#[repr(C, packed)] struct Packed { v: u32 }`. The externs other than `f`"
2605..2677 Comment "// each differ from the row in one clause: `g` takes `n: u64`, `a` takes"
2678..2747 Comment "// `n: Packed`, `h` takes `x: &u32`, `t` takes `x: Tagged`, `b` takes"
2748..2816 Comment "// `x: Option<Box<u32>>`, `w` answers a `u64`, and `k` takes no `n`."
2818..2827 Comment "// `Nat`."
